error[E0404]: this would need an infinite type
 --> mem:///main.lu:2:19
  |
2 |     let f = fn(g) g(g)
  |                   ^ call it `t`: `t` would have to be `fn(_) -> _` with `t` itself inside — the substitution never terminates
  |
  = note: no finite type satisfies a cycle like `t = fn(t) -> …`; this usually means a function is
    applied to itself — name the intended type explicitly to break the cycle.
